Generate dbt documentation for the mart model `{{ model.name }}`.

Return a JSON object with exactly these top-level keys:
- `model_description`: concise one-sentence model description (plain string, no markdown)
- `description_and_motivation`: 2-4 sentences covering grain, purpose, upstream model,
  and typical analyst use cases. Plain text, no markdown headers.
- `known_limitations`: bullet list of edge cases, caveats, data quality issues, or
  filtering decisions a user should be aware of. Use markdown bullet points (- item).
  Write "None identified." if none are known.
- `columns`: object mapping column names to short inline description strings

Column description rules:
- Write short inline descriptions (1-2 sentences max).
- For computed/metric columns, always mention the formula or aggregation used.
- Only generate descriptions for columns where `needs_doc` is true.

Model context:
- layer: {{ model.layer.value }}
- materialized: {{ model.materialized }}
- upstream nodes: {{ model.depends_on_nodes | join(", ") }}

Columns:
{% for column in model.columns.values() %}
- {{ column.name }} (type: {{ column.column_type.value }}, sql_type: {{ column.data_type or "unknown" }})
  needs_doc: {{ column.needs_doc }}
  existing description: {{ column.description or "none" }}
  sql_expression: {{ column.sql_expression or "none" }}
{% endfor %}

Compiled SQL:
{{ model.compiled_code }}